  "mechanismSummary": "NO₂⁺ attacks para to OMe. In one resonance form of the arenium ion the positive charge sits on the carbon bearing OMe, and the oxygen lone pair can then share it (an oxocarbenium ion, every atom with an octet). Attack meta to OMe gives no such form, so ortho/para attack is faster. Ortho nitration also happens; para is usually major on steric grounds.",
